      "path": "$.units[102].text",
      "old": "Everything since came from one demand. The complex derivative must be the same from every direction. On an open region, that makes every small piece of the map a stretch and a turn. It lets boundary values decide the inside. It lets a loop count zeros and poles, and it turns a real integral into a sum of residues. It allows at most one extension to a given connected region, though not always everywhere, and along different paths a continuation can branch.",
      "new": "Everything since came from one demand. The complex derivative must be the same from every direction. On an open region, that makes every small piece of the map a stretch and a turn. It lets boundary values decide the inside. It lets a loop count zeros and poles, and it turns a real integral into a sum of residues. It allows at most one extension to a given connected region, though there may be none, and along different paths a continuation can branch.",
